      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-11T18:33:54Z"
      },
      "message": "docs(process): a contributor's claim must be live - stale after 48 h with nothing behind it\n\nA contributor's claim comment used to stand for as long as the comment\nexisted, so claims whose agents had moved on days ago kept issues locked.\nMaintainer, 2026-11-11: \"unclaim those 8 old ones and let someone pick em\nup and fix em they can't stall\".\n\nAGENTS.md \"A claim comment is a claim\": a contributor's claim is live\nwhile there is an open PR for the issue, a commit on the claimant's\nbranch in the last 48 hours, or a comment by the claimant on the issue in\nthe last 48 hours. Otherwise it is stale: not mirrored, and a `claimed`\nlabel behind it is removed with a comment. A claim also ends when the\nclaimant's last comment withdraws it or the maintainer releases it, and an\nended claim is never mirrored back from its old comment. The 4 h rule for\nthe owner account's own agents is unchanged.\n\nreview-prs step 4 (mirror and withdraw) follows the same rule.\nPROCESS_VERSION 13 -> 14.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
