      "message": "docs(process): stale claims - review fixes\n\n- A stale-release comment ends the claim; a later comment by the claimant\n  does not revive it, only a new claim line does.\n- \"Held by someone else\" needs a LIVE earlier claim; a stale or ended one\n  holds nothing (AGENTS.md \"Mirror it\", review-prs step 4).\n- \"Claim before any code\" names the second exception to \"never work a\n  claimed issue\": a contributor's withdrawn, released or stale claim.\n- The 2026-11-08 quote's last sentence is marked superseded.\n- A P? issue is never relabelled by the sweep, stale claim or not.\n- The skill's ended-claim wordings match AGENTS.md; liveness counts only\n  the claimant's own PR; the fork commit lookup names the claimant's login\n  and what an error means.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
